Engine3D::InvalidateTextureDataCache at NVIDIA's register.

The waiting variant of the texture data cache invalidation (used by
dkCmdBufBarrier with DkBarrier_Tiles or _Fragments and
DkInvalidateFlags_Image, the barrier for sampling what was just drawn) was
defined at method 0x3DD (byte offset 0xF74), marked theoretical, where
NVIDIA's Maxwell class (open-gpu-doc clb197.h) has nothing; its
INVALIDATE_TEXTURE_DATA_CACHE is byte offset 0x1338, method 0x4CE, as
Mesa's nouveau driver uses it (TEX_CACHE_CTL). So nothing was invalidated:
on the console a texture drawn into and then sampled could come out stale
(Super Mario Sunshine's ground, sky, glyphs and screen copies).

diff --git a/source/maxwell/engine_3d.def b/source/maxwell/engine_3d.def
index 30cdbc1..537314e 100644
--- a/source/maxwell/engine_3d.def
+++ b/source/maxwell/engine_3d.def
@@ -239,14 +239,6 @@ engine _3D 0xB197;
 0x3DA TiledCacheUnknownConfig0;
 0x3DB TiledCacheUnknownConfig1;
 0x3DC TiledCacheUnknownConfig3;
-0x3DD InvalidateTextureDataCache bits (
-	// Theoretical register, same as InvalidateTextureDataCacheNoWfi but with implicit Wfi
-	0 Lines enum (
-		0 All;
-		1 One;
-	);
-	4..25 Tag;
-);
 0x3DE DiscardRenderTarget bits (
 	0    DepthStencil bool;
 	4..6 Color;
@@ -409,6 +401,15 @@ engine _3D 0xB197;
 
 0x4C7 BlendConstant array[4] float;
 
+0x4CE InvalidateTextureDataCache bits (
+	// NVB197_INVALIDATE_TEXTURE_DATA_CACHE (byte offset 0x1338, Mesa's
+	// TEX_CACHE_CTL): InvalidateTextureDataCacheNoWfi with a wait for idle
+	0 Lines enum (
+		0 All;
+		1 One;
+	);
+	4..25 Tag;
+);
 0x4D8 ColorBlendEnable array[8] bool;
 0x4E0 StencilEnable bool;
 0x4E1 StencilFrontOpFail;
